--
-- THE SEVENTH IS WHY THIS WAS NOT A STRING SUBSTITUTION. `populations.BRAIN.description`
-- says "Merges former NEU + PCS", so a literal reading sends PCS to BRAIN. But BRAIN is
-- "Incl. post-concussion, stroke, TBI" -- its PCS is POST-CONCUSSION SYNDROME, while the
-- auditor's PCS is POST-COVID SYNDROMES. The auditor's own ICF profile settles it: PCS is
-- d450/d455/d570/d920 "Fatigue + autonomic -- exertion limits", near-identical to OFS's
-- d450/d455/d470/d920, and precisely populations.COM "Complex/energy-limiting: dysautonomia,
-- LONG COVID, MCAS, ME/CFS, POTS". Mapped to COM on the mechanism. Following the string
-- would have filed long-COVID functional mappings under acquired brain injury -- a wrong
-- population on a disability claim, which is the class of error this project exists to avoid.
