-- The reconciliation finding is answered: close it, naming the ruling that closed it.
-- 'CLOSED-DECIDED', not 'CLOSED'. The first cut of this migration wrote 'CLOSED' and
-- test_db_integrity B06 caught it: gaps.status carries only a SHAPE check
-- (LIKE 'OPEN%' OR LIKE 'CLOSED%'), which 'CLOSED' satisfies, while the VOCABULARY lives
-- in a list in that test -- two homes for one rule, and the looser one is the one the
-- database enforces. 'CLOSED-DECIDED' is the member of that vocabulary this closure
-- actually is: the gap asked for an owner ruling on the crosswalk and an owner ruling is
-- what closed it, rather than a fix or a deletion.
UPDATE gaps SET status = 'CLOSED-DECIDED', updated_at = '2026-09-13 06:30', updated_by_session = 'session_2026-09-13-derivation-handshake',
